Theorem RL-11: same-block allocation reuse — conditions (a) + (b) + (c)

  Preconditions:
    - RL-11 governs same-block reuse per Annex E §AIMS Allocation
      Reuse: a dying value's allocation SHALL be reused for a fresh
      allocation of the same type in the same block iff (a) a Reset precedes
      the Reuse, (b) no intervening instruction may throw, may allocate, or
      may use the dying value or any alias of it
      (project_alias_sources MUST be checked), AND (c) the dying value's
      Uniqueness = Unique (non-unique reuse corrupts aliases).
    - Signature ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction per
      the canonical proof notation:264; discharged against the sec-01
      Realization.proof sorry obligation.
    - Reuse eligibility is DP-6 (is_reuse_candidate) <=> Access = Owned AND
      Uniqueness != Shared AND Shape != NonReusable. RL-11 additionally
      requires the dying value Unique (condition c).
    - Shipped: emit_reuse/detect.rs + emit_reuse/planner.rs;
      realize/mod.rs::realize_rc_reuse Sub-step C (emit_reuse_from_events,
      lines 143-167).
    - depends-on sec-05: DP-6 (is_reuse_candidate) soundness; depends-on
      §AIMS §7 project_alias_sources for the intervening-alias-use check.

  Soundness property:
    Forall dying value v in block B and forall fresh same-type allocation a
    in B:

      (P1) Reuse decision: RL-11 reuses v's allocation for a iff DP-6(v) AND
           (a) Reset-precedes-Reuse AND (b) no-intervening-hazard AND
           (c) Uniqueness(v) = Unique.

      (P2) Value-semantics preservation: when (a)+(b)+(c) hold, v is the
           provable sole owner at death (Unique) with no live alias observing
           the reused bytes (no intervening hazard), so reusing v's
           allocation for a is observably equivalent to a fresh allocation
           plus a separate free of v.

    RL-11 refines plain ARC by eliminating the alloc-free pair when the
    lattice proves the dying allocation can carry the fresh value, while
    preserving the same observable behavior.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the case_analysis engine via finite
    enumeration of the (a)+(b)+(c) condition grid + DP-6 cross-check.

    Part (P1/P2) — condition grid:
      abc_all_hold_reuse -> reuse fires (sound)
      no_reset_no_reuse -> (a) violated, no reuse
      intervening_hazard_no_reuse -> (b) violated, no reuse
      non_unique_no_reuse -> (c) violated, no reuse
      Coverage gate: 4 condition cases. Negative-direction witness: a Shared
      dying value is never reuse-eligible (DP-6 excludes Shared) — asserted.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — section_08::verify_rl11_same_block_reuse;
        condition-grid enumeration + DP-6 cross-check; emits Fail on a
        condition divergence or an unsound reuse)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 case_analysis engine discharges RL-11 via the same-block reuse condition grid (a) Reset-precedes-Reuse (b) no-intervening-hazard (c) dying-Unique, each cross-checked against DP-6 reuse-eligibility, with a negative-direction witness rejecting a Shared dying value, grounded in the shipped emit_reuse/detect.rs + planner.rs reuse-from-events realization
